{"index":0,"content":"\n\n<think>\nThe user wants a C++20 function that:\n1. Validates balanced brackets (round, square, curly)\n2. Ignores brackets inside quoted strings (both single and double quotes)\n3. Includes a compact self-test\n4. Returns code only\n\nLet me think about the design:\n\n- I need to track whether I'm inside a string (single or double quoted)\n- Handle escape characters (backslash) inside strings\n- Use a stack for bracket matching\n- Brackets to check: (), [], {}\n\nEdge cases:\n- Escaped quotes inside strings: \"she said \\\"hi\\\"\"\n- Escaped backslashes: \"path\\\\to\"\n- Unterminated strings - should I treat that as invalid? I'll say yes, if we're still in a string at the end, it's invalid.\n- Nested strings? In C++, you can't really nest same-type strings, but you can have single quotes in double-quoted strings and vice versa.\n\nLet me write this:\n\n```cpp\n#include <string>\n#include <stack>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <iostream>\n\nbool balanced(const std::string& s) {\n    std::stack<char> st;\n    char quote = 0; // 0 = not in string, ' = in single, \" = in double\n    bool escape = false;\n    \n    for (char c : s) {\n        if (quote) {\n            if (escape) { escape = false; continue; }\n            if (c == '\\\\') { escape = true; continue; }\n            if (c == quote) { quote = 0; continue; }\n            continue; // ignore everything in string\n        }\n        \n        if (c == '\"' || c == '\\'') {\n            quote = c;\n            continue;\n        }\n        \n        if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') {\n            st.push(c);\n        } else if (c == ')' || c == ']' || c == '}') {\n            if (st.empty()) return false;\n            char top = st.top(); st.pop();\n            if ((c == ')' && top != '(') ||\n                (c == ']' && top != '[') ||\n                (c == '}' && top != '{')) return false;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    return st.empty()","tokens":[],"id_slot":0,"stop":true,"model":"qwen3.8-27b@q4_k_m","tokens_predicted":512,"tokens_evaluated":28,"generation_settings":{"seed":202,"temperature":0.6000000238418579,"dynatemp_range":0.0,"dynatemp_exponent":1.0,"top_k":20,"top_p":0.949999988079071,"min_p":0.0,"top_n_sigma":-1.0,"xtc_probability":0.0,"xtc_threshold":0.10000000149011612,"typical_p":1.0,"repeat_last_n":64,"repeat_penalty":1.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"dry_multiplier":0.0,"dry_base":1.75,"dry_allowed_length":2,"dry_penalty_last_n":64,"dry_sequence_breakers":["\n",":","\"","*"],"mirostat":0,"mirostat_tau":5.0,"mirostat_eta":0.10000000149011612,"adaptive_target":-1.0,"adaptive_decay":0.8999999761581421,"stop":[],"max_tokens":512,"n_predict":512,"n_keep":0,"n_discard":0,"ignore_eos":false,"stream":false,"logit_bias":[],"n_probs":0,"min_keep":0,"grammar":"","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[],"chat_format":"Content-only","reasoning_format":"auto","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none,draft-mtp","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":true,"lora":[]},"prompt":"Write a C++20 function that validates balanced brackets while ignoring brackets inside quoted strings. Include a compact self-test. Return code only.","has_new_line":true,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"limit","stopping_word":"","tokens_cached":539,"timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":28,"prompt_ms":199.313,"prompt_per_token_ms":7.118321428571428,"prompt_per_second":140.48255758530553,"predicted_n":512,"predicted_ms":8690.271,"predicted_per_token_ms":17.0064011741683,"predicted_per_second":58.801388357164,"draft_n":555,"draft_n_accepted":371}}